From f2de3717c57630ce566fcef476cab3c9ff7a85cb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: zimbermanne <zimbermanne@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 30 Jul 2026 09:30:53 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Mobile: make the app feel native, not a shrunk desktop site

Finishes and adds the concrete things that made mobile feel like a
scaled-down desktop layout instead of a real mobile app:

- Add bottom tab bar (BottomNav.jsx) for one-tap access to the most
  used destinations (Home, POS, Sales, Debtors), matching the native
  app tab-bar pattern instead of everything living two taps deep in
  the hamburger drawer.
- Finish the responsive-table feature: Table.jsx already carried
  data-label attributes and a responsive-table class, but the CSS to
  actually turn a table into stacked label/value cards on phones was
  never written, so it silently did nothing. Added the mobile
  breakpoint rules that make each row render as a card instead of a
  cramped, horizontally-scrolling grid.
- Tighten .page/.card padding on mobile (24px/18px desktop density
  was carrying straight through to phones).
- Switch modals from a small centered desktop dialog to a full-width
  bottom sheet that slides up, with safe-area padding for notched
  phones -- the single most obvious 'this is just a shrunk desktop
  popup' tell.
- Shrink the page-header h1 size to fit phone widths without wrapping
  awkwardly.
---
